      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & -3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -11 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -11 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -11 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -7 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=\\frac{1}{2}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -7 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z&=-3 \\\\ y+2z&=-1 \\\\ z&=-2\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-2 \\\\ y&=-1-(2)(-2)=3 \\\\ x&=-3-(1)(3)-(2)(-2)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -2,3,-2\\rangle$.",
